lines=['# BICG: closed P0/F128/F256 six-source comparison','', '**Finding:** F256 recovers part of DH\'s F128 regression, but does not recover its own P0 performance or catch CH. DH P0/F128/F256 cycles are28,685,812 /29,210,480 /28,883,488. CH cycles are26,298,698 /24,464,891 /24,651,923. Relative to F128, F256 saves DH326,992cycles but costs CH187,032cycles; all these cycle changes occur in K2, with exactly unchanged K1 in each design.','', 'This packet is one input with six matched closed sources. It does not select per-program best configurations for a GM, modify old results, or consume the currently active scan/MVT runs. Both new CH points independently passed the frozen read-only strict/archive/native-restore audit. Original F128 packet bytes remain unchanged; its historical OO-prefixed CH diagnostic naming error is not reused. The typed mapping here follows the forward clarification: CH common and DH OO are separate domains.','', '## Exact identity and actual trace contract','', 'Input `ae34174fbbdf83b20a72f44492665cf4b99ed35563f482f7d14763e89f398aef`. The canonical input binding, full declared-body qualification, actual strict proof/raw kernel boundaries and bounded4096-byte headers agree: K1 `_Z12bicg_kernel1PfS_S_` has74,285,056active-thread instructions; K2 `_Z12bicg_kernel2PfS_S_` has71,380,992. Both grid(16,1,1),block(256,1,1),16CTAs, stream0; total145,666,048instructions and32CTAs. The order/instruction split is BICG\'s own, not copied from ATAX/MVT.','', 'Core `9eedb3131937748f0492fa83aad37d3691118d70`, Framework `02775fd795cde5aae1480d81cee6eb481d0a08f4`, binary SHA `02a289360b42a573832698c978f21ad2125182a453067a35be60410f1eb8888d`. Original references are exact full-digest/cell/profile rows from ORIGINAL_REFERENCE_INDEX.json; no same-name R2/IR/EP/PQPS result is substituted. Any inherited P0 reference alias remains disclosed. New CH has its authorized StageII role. The prior F128 manifest `f2b1dfc69e860b56e96ec70f50490458d843a8808f5f7d598852571790401cba` and every member SHA were rechecked unchanged; all four former RESULT identities remain exact.','', '## Performance, including unfavorable outcomes','',tab(['Profile','CH cycles','DH cycles','S_CH=CH0/CH_F','S_DH=DH0/DH_F','CH_F/DH_F','I=S_DH/S_CH','DH extra cycles vs same-F CH %'],[[p,by['CH',p]['cycles'],by['DH',p]['cycles'],1 if p=='P0'else next(x['S_CH']for x in perf if x['profile']==p),1 if p=='P0'else next(x['S_DH']for x in perf if x['profile']==p),by['CH',p]['cycles']/by['DH',p]['cycles'],1 if p=='P0'else next(x['I']for x in perf if x['profile']==p),100*(by['DH',p]['cycles']/by['CH',p]['cycles']-1)]for p in['P0','F128','F256']]),'', 'F256 vs P0: CH gains1.066801x in reciprocal cycles, DH has0.993156x (0.6891% more cycles). F256 DH still needs17.1653% more cycles than matched CH. F128 DH is1.8290% slower than its P0 and19.3975% slower than CH. I is below1 for both F profiles, so the coupled downstream expansion worsens DTC\'s relative position to CH compared with P0, even though F256 improves that position relative to F128.','',tab(['Source','K1 cycles','K2 cycles','K1 delta vs P0','K2 delta vs P0'],[[c+'-'+p,by[c,p]['kernels'][0]['cycles'],by[c,p]['kernels'][1]['cycles'],by[c,p]['kernels'][0]['cycles']-by[c,'P0']['kernels'][0]['cycles'],by[c,p]['kernels'][1]['cycles']-by[c,'P0']['kernels'][1]['cycles']]for c,p in pairs]),'', 'Fixed candidate BICG source maps K1 to s=A^T*r with lane-contiguous A and broadcast r, and K2 to q=A*p with row-strided A across lanes and broadcast p (`bicg.cu:99-113;117-131;launch166-196`). This explains the access-direction contrast to test; it does not certify capture ELF/numeric semantics or establish the causal bottleneck. Unlike ATAX, these source operations use separate vectors and do not make q consume s. Current runtime cycle evidence locates F sensitivity in K2.','', '## Legal cumulative traffic and retry counters','', 'L2 GLOBAL accepted/miss units are32-byte sectors. Accepted excludes retry events; misses=MISS+SECTOR_MISS. DRAM reads/writes are issued32-byte data atoms summed over20controllers; these are not generally one-to-one with every L2 access type. All-L2 misses include non-GLOBAL-read types. All values are explicit cumulative final stream0 snapshots; they are never summed over kernels.','']
keys=[('L2_GLOBAL_read_accepted_sectors','L2 GLOBAL accepted read sectors'),('L2_GLOBAL_read_miss_sectors','L2 GLOBAL read miss sectors'),('L2_total_cache_misses','All-L2 miss sectors'),('DRAM_issued_read_atoms32B','DRAM read atoms32B'),('DRAM_issued_write_atoms32B','DRAM write atoms32B'),('L2_total_cache_reservation_fails','All-L2 retry events'),('gpu_stall_dramfull','ICNT-to-memory blocked-admission events')]
lines+=[tab(['Counter',*[c+'-'+p for c,p in pairs]],[[name,*[by[c,p]['totals'].get(k)for c,p in pairs]]for k,name in keys]),'', 'F256 relative to F128, same-design differences:','',tab(['Design','Counter','F128','F256','Delta','Change %'],[[x['cell'],name,*[x['counter_changes'][k][v]for v in['F128','F256','delta','pct']]]for x in profile_diffs if x['stage']=='TOTAL'for k,name in keys]),'', 'DH-F256 becomes faster than F128 while OO lower creations and accepted L2 reads increase5.26%, issued DRAM reads fall2.77%, writes rise6.65%, and aggregate retry/admission events rise0.095%/0.60%. Hence fewer lower requests, fewer retries or universally lower traffic cannot serve as a single explanation. CH-F256 becomes slower than F128 while accepted reads, read misses, retries and admission blocks rise, but its writes decline. These are observed associations, not isolated causes.','', 'Print-boundary kernel interval differences require both cumulative endpoints explicitly present. They are not automatically request-origin labels; means/gauges/peaks are never differenced. The raw-derived interval table preserves all six sources:','',tab(['Source','Interval','L2 GLOBAL accepted','GLOBAL misses','DRAM reads32B','DRAM writes32B','All-L2 retries','ICNT admission blocks'],[[c+'-'+p,k['ordinal'],*[k['print_boundary_interval_additive'].get(key)for key in['L2_GLOBAL_read_accepted_sectors','L2_GLOBAL_read_miss_sectors','DRAM_issued_read_atoms32B','DRAM_issued_write_atoms32B','L2_total_cache_reservation_fails','gpu_stall_dramfull']]]for c,p in pairs for k in by[c,p]['kernels']]),'', '## Entry and merge retries: remain distinct','']
