lines+=[tab(['Explicit positive-only reason',*[c+'-'+p for c,p in pairs]],[[k,*[by[c,p]['raw_reason_final_explicitly_printed'].get(k)for c,p in pairs]]for k in reasonkeys]),'', 'DH read MISS_QUEUE_FULL drops15,514,452 ->137,002 ->37,513 across P0/F128/F256. Yet MSHR entry-capacity failures remain142,533,205 ->159,204,818 ->159,372,674; F256 is slightly higher than F128 and materially higher than P0. Its entry failures account for most of the aggregate retries, but the count is neither occupancy nor critical-path time. Merge-list failures15,401 ->15,832 ->15,401 belong to an existing-address merge-limit check and must not be conflated with entry exhaustion.','', 'CH read MISS_QUEUE_FULL drops10,086,344 ->6,746 ->64, while entry failures rise39,160,496 ->39,747,955 ->41,521,806. Thus ?miss queue pressure fell? does not establish that a different bottleneck was removed or that increasing entries would improve performance. Retry reasons are positive-only prints; missing entries stay MISSING, never imputed0. They are not stalled-cycle durations or a decomposition of total cycles.','', '## Active frontend and finite service','', 'CH PAPER_BASE uses active common PIB256; DH PAPER_OO uses active OO PIB128. DH generic PIB8 does not set OO admission capacity. Common CH Tag/PIB values are never assigned to OO fields. OO PIB-full and OO Tag-conflict events remain unprinted/null, not copied CH zeros. CH\'s disabled DTC finite-service extension does not mean unlimited ordinary-cache service. These modes differ in L1 structure, Tag, queues, timing and area; all matched-F comparisons preserve that disclosure.','',tab(['Typed event',*[c+'-'+p for c,p in pairs]],[[label,*[by[c,p]['totals'].get(k)for c,p in pairs]]for k,label in [('DTC_L1_tag_conflicts','CH common Tag-bank conflict attempts'),('DTC_L1_pib_full_events','CH common PIB-full events'),('DTC_L1_oo_valid_hits','DH OO valid-line hits'),('DTC_L1_oo_pending_hits','DH OO pending-line hits'),('DTC_L1_oo_new_misses','DH OO new-line misses'),('DTC_L1_oo_lower_created','DH OO128B lower creations'),('DTC_L1_oo_tag_evictions','DH OO tag-map evictions')]]),'', 'DH valid+pending+new classifications conserve18,350,080line probes for all three profiles. New misses=lower created=issued=responses=lower credits acquired/released; L2 GLOBAL accepted sectors=4*128B lower creations. F256 relative to F128 has fewer valid hits and more new misses/evictions, yet fewer DRAM reads and faster cycles. OO Tag classification is therefore not interchangeable with DRAM misses or a direct performance prediction.','',tab(['DH profile','Mean PIB entries, all64SM samples','Mean physical lines','Ready-to-retire cycles / retired entry','Map-loss-to-free cycles / event'],[[p,*[next(x for x in typed if x['cell']=='DH'and x['profile']==p)['DH_finite_service'][k]for k in['mean_PIB_entries_across_all64SMs','mean_physical_lines_across_all64SMs','fully_ready_to_retire_cycles_per_retired_entry','map_loss_to_free_cycles_per_recorded_event']]]for p in['P0','F128','F256']]),'', 'Finite-service retired denominator is2,097,152 in all profiles. F256 ready-to-complete sum9,101,167 remains above P0 9,069,203 but slightly below F128 9,125,347; writeback waits32,826 /34,394 /32,432 are not monotonic. Each ratio uses its own additive numerator/denominator; these sample/entry means are not critical-path durations or proofs that bursts/per-SM bottlenecks are absent. Terminal gauges and running peaks remain separate in the source data.','', '## Latency windows and F coupling','',tab(['Source','Reported mflatency','Reported ICNT-to-memory','Reported ICNT-to-shader','Reported MRQ'],[[c+'-'+p,*[by[c,p]['strict_latency_counters'].get(k)for k in['averagemflatency','avg_icnt2mem_latency','avg_icnt2sh_latency','avg_mrq_latency']]]for c,p in pairs]),'', 'These are integer printed diagnostics with500,000cycle sample/print/update-tail limitations; never sum/difference them over kernels or reinterpret missing as0. MRQ is a separate cumulative request-denominator mean from DRAM-request construction to bank assignment in global core cycles, not complete L2-to-DRAM latency or critical dependency wait. DH MRQ791 ->1477 ->2074 increases even as F256 improves over F128. Existing means do not establish that a larger F reduced average DRAM queue wait. CH/DH means need not cover equal request populations.','', 'Within each design only FR-FCFS size64/128/256 changes. Fixed Core simultaneously changes memory-partition shared-credit limits255/319/447 (`FR_queue+return_queue192-(subpartitions2-1)`), not a pure isolated queue capacity. DRAM850MHz, Core/ICNT/L2 clocks,10MiB L2 capacity/mapping and each design\'s frontend remain fixed. High resources are not free/equal-area hardware.','', '## Evidence levels and unresolved cause','', 'Fact: all F sensitivity in BICG total cycles is K2, with CH helped by both F variants and DH still worse than P0. F256 vs F128 improves DH despite higher lower-request and retry populations. Association: coupled scheduling/credits alter reuse, miss/service and arrival patterns. Hypothesis only: those timing/lifetime changes redistribute residency/overlap in the strided K2; current aggregates do not isolate banks, credits, queue occupancy or critical dependent requests. Do not infer entry expansion as a guaranteed remedy from a dominant retry count.','', 'The fixed candidate source is Atlas47a097aad4406893a07f8d230e1e0a850609bf39 / app commitdad09cb0487845edc7524ded814c6cde9f0ef6a1, `BICG/bicg.cu` SHAc38c3b0bb1a543ce37ee6d4d7abe433a36574f05b49574e6bf1004c45b68f6fe, kernel99-131/launch166-196. This is exact recovered source, not a certified capture-time ELF/numeric linkage. Current full declared-body coverage does not newly certify full native application semantics or numerical correctness. Source-derived address repeats are not measured cache hits or MSHR merges.','', 'No new experiment, remaining48batch, trace, source modification, controller action or paper change is authorized by this analysis. A causal time-resolved attribution would need separately authorized observation; this packet only consumes existing closed evidence.','', '## Reproduction and source locators','', 'Run `python3 analyze_three_profiles.py`, `python3 validate_and_derive.py`, then `python3 render_three_profiles.py` only to regenerate this new packet. SIX_CLOSED_SOURCE_DATA.json retains all exact RESULT, raw gzip/uncompressed and NATIVE_EXIT SHA, UUIDs, original roles/aliases, complete options, cumulative counters, explicit-endpoint intervals, raw reasons, means/gauges/peaks. F256_VS_F128_COUNTERS.json makes the direct F comparison reproducible. BICG_FIXED_SOURCE_PHASE_MAPPING.json pins source/header/trace boundaries. The typed-domain and input-contract files preserve active capacities/nulls. F128_PIN_CONSUMPTION.json preserves the old package manifest and exact unmodified members; its historical named diagnostic error is documented, not silently overwritten.','',f"CPU_VALIDATION.json: {v['count']}checks PASS; two new CH archive/strict/native-restore independent audits PASS; no live points consumed or model actions. MANIFEST.json freezes every public member.",'',tab(['Source','RESULT path','RESULT SHA256','UUID','Raw gzip SHA256'],[[c+'-'+p,by[c,p]['RESULT_path'],by[c,p]['RESULT_sha256'],by[c,p]['uuid'],by[c,p]['raw_gzip_sha256']]for c,p in pairs]),'']
